  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The\r\nproposed development, by reason of an absence of a needs assessment fails to\r\njustify the loss of a family dwellinghouse and a change of use to a C2 use\r\nspecifically for children’s care home. In the absence of sufficient information\r\nsubmitted, the development proposal falls contrary to guidance contained within\r\nthe National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy H12 of the London Plan\r\n(2021), and Policy HO7 of the London Borough of Harrow New Local Plan\r\n(2021-2041).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design (lack of defensible space and access control system) and absent details on security or safety of the children or staff, fails to demonstrate Secured By Design Principles.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;In the absence of sufficient information and failure to demonstrate changes capable of being adapted for inclusivity and the changing needs of a building’s occupants over its lifetime, the proposal, as submitted, fails to adhere with Policy GR3A(C)(D) of the London Borough of Harrow New Local Plan (2021-2041), Policies D5 and D11 of the London Plan (2021) and Secured by Design Residential (Homes) Guide: Edition 1 (2025) and guidance contained under Para 90 of the ‘National Planning Policy Framework’ (2024).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of absent details on soundproofing, insulation and/or other acoustic design measures in facilitating the use class change, fails to demonstrate how noise and other potential nuisances are to be managed.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;In the absence of sufficient information submitted, the proposal falls contrary to Policies D13 and D14 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy GR1 of the London Borough of Harrow New Local Plan (2021-2041).&amp;nbsp;"
  ],
